// The kernel refuses a term-mode theorem with no register row (ADR 2.10.26d AC 4).
//
// A record theorem: the elaborator accepts `refl`, but the record reaches the
// kernel as a bare name it cannot bind. This golden used `two_is_two`'s shape
// until ADR 2.10.26l taught the kernel to unfold `two`; since ADR 3.10.26p a
// record reaches the kernel by its encoding, so `Point` is self-recursive — a
// cycle the presentation leaves named (D3).
// With no row, the build fails with E0081, naming the theorem and its cause.
type Point = { x: Nat, next: Link }

type Link = End | More(Point)

fn px(p: Point) -> Nat { p.x }

theorem px_refl(p: Point): px(p) == px(p) { refl }
